use dacc_core::{NonEmptyStr, nonempty_str};

dacc_knowledge::review!("v0014",
    title: NonEmptyStr::new("A second hand reads the invariants promoted by the first"),
    angle: NonEmptyStr::new("A read of the thirteen invariants W-012 names as promoted to `enforced` by the same hand that wrote them: each entry's adversarial test is held against the bypass its own entry names, by reading the test in the code rather than the anchor in the entry."),
    findings: nonempty_str![
        "major — INV-SECRET-003's adversarial test did not attempt the bypass its entry names, and this is exactly the failure class W-012 and RULES.md:42-49 exist to catch. The entry's bypass is 'a provider handed a credential recovered from state, which is only possible if state held one' (doc/invariant/i0033.rs:6), but the test it pointed at — a_password_reaches_the_file_and_nothing_else — exercises the apply path: the plan and the state file do not carry the password, and the file on the machine does (crates/nerpa-provider-os/tests/secret.rs:109). That is INV-SECRET-001 and INV-SECRET-002; it never touches the path this entry claims, which is `Record::locator` dropping digests when a provider reads a resource back from state to remove it or find it (crates/nerpa-core/src/state.rs:158). Fixed rather than demoted, because the guarantee holds and the missing attempt was the only gap: a_record_handed_back_to_a_provider_holds_no_secret (crates/nerpa-core/tests/secret.rs) builds a record holding a path and a secret, calls locator, and asserts the path survives while the secret does not. The entry now points at that test.",
        "strength — the other twelve matched. Each remaining adversarial test was read in the code and held against the bypass its entry names: the secret accessor (i0031), the keyed digests (i0032), the function-parameter comparison (i0034), the unreadable/non-text/symlink reads (i0035), the non-empty-directory and symlink removals (i0036), the reserved-map and text-versus-bytes round trip (i0037), the empty-configuration substitution (i0038), the shared-across-threads provider (i0041), the unreported attribute (i0043), the plan-number coverage (i0044), the template boundary (i0051) and the moved premise (i0052). In each, the test asserts the refusal says what it refuses, not only that it fired.",
        "verdict — one finding, and it was a test pointing at the wrong guarantee rather than a guarantee with nothing behind it. The two that W-012 says a second read turned back to `claimed` on the day they left it had their lesson taken: the check is now a second hand's job, and this one found one entry still carrying the first hand's shortcut.",
    ],
    authors: nonempty_str!["An independent reader — an agent that wrote none of the entries"],
    decided_at: dacc_core::date!(2026, 10, 7),
);
